Intern real-container verification runtime

The runtime derives from the official docker.io/library/mysql image locked in
app/cli/internal/qualitygate/contract.json. MySQL Community Server and its client
utilities are Oracle software distributed under GNU GPL version 2 and applicable
additional licenses. Upstream notices in the base image are retained. The
unmodified mysqlbinlog executable is extracted from the official, versioned
mysql-community-client RPM; its LICENSE and README are retained under
/usr/share/licenses/intern/mysql-community-client/.

Official binary/source distribution and license information:
https://dev.mysql.com/downloads/mysql/
https://downloads.mysql.com/archives/community/
https://github.com/mysql/mysql-server
https://github.com/docker-library/mysql

The exact binary RPM URLs/checksums and base image digests are recorded in
app/cli/internal/qualitygate/contract.json. The cpio extractor is used only in a
build stage, not added to the final image by this Dockerfile.

This repository's workflow builds and exercises a private test candidate; it
neither publishes this image nor represents a completed redistributor source
code offer. Before external distribution, provide the corresponding source or
other GPL-compliant source provision, and all required third-party notices for
the chosen exact versions. A link alone is not claimed to satisfy every
redistribution obligation. See docs/roadmap/数据库备份与恢复-2026-10-17.md, sections 10 and 15.

Physical runner admission and verification (P2, issue #27):
github.com/hashicorp/go-version v1.9.0 is used under MPL-2.0; its upstream
LICENSE is retained by the Go module distribution:
https://github.com/hashicorp/go-version/blob/v1.9.0/LICENSE
The real-component harness reuses testcontainers-go v0.44.0 (MIT).
It executes the unmodified percona/percona-xtrabackup:8.4.0-7 image pinned
in internal/physical/compat.json. Percona XtraBackup is GPLv2 software:
https://github.com/percona/percona-xtrabackup
These tests do not publish an Intern runtime image or fulfill the separate
D1 redistribution/source-provision acceptance requirement.
The P2 login-path isolation fixture also executes the unmodified
mysql_config_editor from the matching official client RPM, using the existing
client-tools Dockerfile target and the checksum-pinned CLI profile for that
same MySQL image. The native tool, not a reimplemented login-file codec, creates
the fixture. This helper image is not published.

Plain FTP repository and real-server verification (S1, issue #28):
github.com/jlaffaye/ftp v0.2.4 is used under ISC:
https://github.com/jlaffaye/ftp/blob/v0.2.4/LICENSE
The private fixture builds unmodified Pure-FTPd 1.0.54 with quota support
from its official release tarball, verified against the SHA512 pinned in
app/web/integration/ftp.Dockerfile. Pure-FTPd is ISC-licensed:
https://github.com/jedisct1/pure-ftpd/blob/1.0.54/COPYING
The image retains COPYING at /usr/share/licenses/pure-ftpd/COPYING.
The exact Alpine base digest and build/runtime package versions are pinned
in that Dockerfile. Alpine package license information remains upstream:
https://pkgs.alpinelinux.org/
The fixture uses Pure-FTPd's built-in system crypt path with musl 1.2.6-r3
(MIT), not the optional libsodium backend. Generated test credentials must
use the upstream default bcrypt cost 10; an unexpected fallback is refused.
https://pkgs.alpinelinux.org/package/v3.24/main/x86_64/musl
https://git.musl-libc.org/cgit/musl/tree/COPYRIGHT?h=v1.2.6
This fixture is used only for private verification, not published as an
Intern runtime image. SFTPGo was evaluated but is not the selected fixture:
its quota/permission status codes did not match the locked fault scenarios.
